       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Acetaminophen 5000 mg three times daily comes to 15 g/day. The usual maximum for an adult is 4 g/day, and many institutions cap it at 3 g/day. A single 5 g dose is also well above the usual 1 g maximum. At this dose, the risk of serious hepatotoxicity and liver failure is high, even with normal liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- 500 mg PO three times daily (1.5 g/day)\n- 650 mg PO three times daily (1.95 g/day)\n- 1000 mg PO three times daily (3 g/day)\n\nIf you do want 5000 mg per dose, please confirm that and give me the clinical rationale. I can then enter it with a note, though I'd still advise against it. Otherwise, tell me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
      }
