     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. Acetaminophen 5000 mg three times daily is 15 g/day. That is a toxic dose, and a single 5 g dose can cause hepatotoxicity. I know of no indication that would justify it, and normal liver and kidney function doesn't change that. I can't enter an order I expect to seriously harm the patient.\n\nIf I've misunderstood the clinical situation, I can still help in these ways:\n- **Enter a standard dose.** For example, 1000 mg PO three times daily (3 g/day) or 650 mg PO every 6 hours. Give me the dose and I'll enter it.\n- **Treat a suspected overdose.** If this is about an overdose, the treatment is N-acetylcysteine, guided by a nomogram and acetaminophen levels, along with poison control. I can help enter that order.\n- **Escalate through pharmacy.** If you believe there's a real reason for this dose, please talk to the pharmacist or the clinical decision support team directly.\n\nWhich of these would you like?"
      }
     ],
